            "key": "jamdani",
            "number": "10",
            "title": "Jamdani",
            "summary": "Motifs introduced by hand as the cloth is woven.",
            "tagline": "Motifs within the weave",
            "body": "<p>Jamdani patterns are introduced by hand during weaving. The motifs are part of the cloth as it is made, rather than a print applied afterwards. A close view of the loom makes the relationship between the fine ground and the pattern visible.</p>",
